{"id": "q0218", "pool": "hard-knowledge", "tier": "aggressive", "audio_s": 16.71, "n_chunks": 17, "scores": [0.4789, 0.535, 0.4164, 0.6875, 0.4879, 0.4329, 0.2837, 0.4171, 0.4475, 0.47, 0.3123, 0.2668, 0.3534, 0.5124, 0.3741, 0.3405, 0.4468], "eot_score": 0.6818, "eot_read_ms": 20, "reference_answer": "C. price = minimum average variable cost.", "query": "Which of the following is not correct for the perfectly competitive firm, in the long run?\n\nA. price = marginal revenue.\nB. price = minimum average cost.\nC. price = minimum average variable cost.\nD. price = marginal cost.\n\nAnswer with the correct option letter and its content.", "transcript": "Which of the following is not correct for the perfectly competitive firm in the long run? a) Price equals marginal revenue. b) Price equals minimum average cost. c) Price minimum average variable cost. d) Price equals marginal cost. Answer with the correct option letter and its content:", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The answer is C. Price minimum average variable cost.", "expert_answer": "c) Price minimum average variable cost.", "expert_latency_s": 2.93, "stall_ms": 25, "relay_ms": 259}
